      <link>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/perl-weekly-challenge-401/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://theweeklychallenge.org/blog/perl-weekly-challenge-401/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;table-of-contents&#34;&gt;TABLE OF CONTENTS&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;1-headlines&#34;&gt;  1. &lt;a href=&#34;#HEADLINES&#34;&gt;HEADLINES&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;2-sponsor&#34;&gt;  2. &lt;a href=&#34;#SPONSOR&#34;&gt;SPONSOR&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;3-recap&#34;&gt;  3. &lt;a href=&#34;#RECAP&#34;&gt;RECAP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;4-perl-review&#34;&gt;  4. &lt;a href=&#34;#PERLREVIEW&#34;&gt;PERL REVIEW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;5-raku-review&#34;&gt;  5. &lt;a href=&#34;#RAKUREVIEW&#34;&gt;RAKU REVIEW&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;6-chart&#34;&gt;  6. &lt;a href=&#34;#CHART&#34;&gt;CHART&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;7-new-members&#34;&gt;  7. &lt;a href=&#34;#NEWMEMBERS&#34;&gt;NEW MEMBERS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;8-guests&#34;&gt;  8. &lt;a href=&#34;#GUESTS&#34;&gt;GUESTS&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;9-task-1-fractional-addition-substraction&#34;&gt;  9. &lt;a href=&#34;#TASK1&#34;&gt;TASK #1: Fractional Addition Substraction&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;10-task-2-reconstruct-digits&#34;&gt;10. &lt;a href=&#34;#TASK2&#34;&gt;TASK #2: Reconstruct Digits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;HEADLINES&#34;&gt;HEADLINES&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Welcome to the &lt;code&gt;Week #401&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;code&gt;The Weekly Challenge&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Welcome aboard, &lt;strong&gt;Caden Young&lt;/strong&gt;, and thanks for your first contributions in &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/manwar/perlweeklychallenge-club/tree/master/challenge-400/caden-young&#34;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Perl&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;With regret, I announce &lt;strong&gt;Peter Campbell Smith&lt;/strong&gt; has decided to formally retire from active contributions to the weekly challenge. He has been with us for a very long time even after retirement from regular job. He has been declared champions twice during this period, first in &lt;strong&gt;December 2021&lt;/strong&gt; and then in &lt;strong&gt;February 2025&lt;/strong&gt;. He is currently ranked &lt;strong&gt;#15&lt;/strong&gt; in the leaderboard. He has been inspirational for me. I really wanted to lead an active &lt;strong&gt;Perl&lt;/strong&gt; contribution life post retirement like him. The format of the weekly challenge is such that you are not tied to it. You are free to take a break and come back when you are available. I have seen members taking a short break and coming back with full energy. I hope and wish &lt;strong&gt;Peter&lt;/strong&gt; might come back again.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
